        },
        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit coverage for lod_declare_layout_set/del",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit coverage for lod_declare_layout_set/del\n\nAdd KUnit coverage for lod_declare_layout_set() and\nlod_declare_layout_del(), the \"lfs setstripe --component-flags\" and\n\"--component-del\" entry points. Both only walk/mutate an object's\nexisting ldo_comp_entries[] array and declare the resulting LOVEA on\ndt_object_child(dt), so a bare struct lod_object with a hand-built\nstatic component array and the shared mock_ost_obj \"next\" object is\nenough; no real OST/OSP is needed.\n\nlod_declare_layout_set()/_del() leave info->lti_buf.lb_buf unset when\ndeclaring the new LOVEA xattr (only lb_len is set), since real\n->do_declare_xattr_set() OSD implementations only consult the length\nto reserve transaction credits. Exercising that call convention\nagainst mock_ost_obj_declare_xattr_set() crashed with a NULL pointer\ndereference, because the mock unconditionally memcpy()'d from\nbuf->lb_buf to record it for the test to inspect. Fix the mock to\ntreat a NULL buf->lb_buf as valid, matching real declare-only\nbackends, recording a NULL/len pair instead of crashing. Also add the\nmock's missing do_declare_xattr_del() op, needed by the \"del\" with no\nremaining components test case.\n\nExport lod_declare_layout_set()/lod_declare_layout_del() and declare\nthem in lod_internal.h so the test module can call them directly.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5 [augment-code]\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I42d558755b7defebc09bbc1d1a16945d76216491\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
